de you got to be ready to  go march 18  when the free agency period opens in the  new league year begins  you know with with danny dalton uh it  all really reminds me of the ryan  tannehill situation from last year and i  don't think they get a whole lot for him  i think he goes somewhere where he could  be a backup quarterback  and you know the team that came to mind  right away when i heard this was the  chicago bears go back him up and and if  your starting quarterback starts to fail  you go hey we got a better guy sitting  there on the bench let's see what this  guy can do and i do think andy dalton  can play i see him going somewhere as a  backup quarterback i don't see him going  somewhere where he's gonna start uh as  come in as the guy who's gonna start for  that team so if you're gonna do that  you're not gonna get a first round pick  you're not gonna get a second round pick  so i it so reminds me of the ryan  tannehill situation and i think he goes  somewhere to a team that's looking at  that backup that maybe can come in and  take over if that starter starts to  struggle a little bit  here's the one caveat i'll apply to that  though shireen in this looming game of  quarterback musical chairs i still don't  think we know whether when the music  stops there's going to be more butts  than seats or more seats than butts and  there's a chance that there's going to  be a team  that is left because they waited too  long to have something lined up they're  going to be left looking around saying  who the hell is our quarterback for  2020. and if there's an andy dalton  that's still available in trade if  there's a philip rivers who is still  available in free agency that's when  maybe you end up getting more because  you waited because there's a team or two  out there that all of a sudden is  desperate and i keep coming back to the  patriots right they get left high and  try and i think this is why they want to  know what tom brady is going to do  because they're 